---
/**
 * The list that holds <Role> cards. Layout only — every word lives in the post.
 *
 * This was a four-column table with a second stacked layout below 900px. It is
 * cards now: unlike the figure, this content genuinely reflows, so it needs one
 * layout rather than two. Dropping `<table>` also drops `display: block` on
 * table/tr/td, which strips table semantics in some assistive tech.
 *
 * `not-prose` keeps Tailwind Typography off the cards; the post body is `prose`
 * and would otherwise restyle the slotted markdown inside them.
 */
---

<div class="not-prose roles"><slot /></div>

<style>
  .roles {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    /* block only — the post's wide container centres its children with
       `margin-inline: auto`, and a shorthand here would out-specify it and
       pin the list to the left edge */
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }
</style>
